# ClearPluginAssemblies

`src/Build/ClearPluginAssemblies.dll` and `.runtimeconfig.json` are committed build outputs. `ClearPluginAssemblies.proj` hardcodes `<TargetFramework>` and does not always pick up `Directory.Build.props`.

When you change the helper source or the solution TFM:

1. Update TFM in `src/Build/src/ClearPluginAssemblies/*.csproj` **and** `src/Build/ClearPluginAssemblies.proj`
2. Rebuild and copy outputs into `src/Build/`
3. Commit the new DLL and runtimeconfig with the source change

```bash
dotnet build src/Build/src/ClearPluginAssemblies/ClearPluginAssemblies.csproj -c Release
cp -f src/Build/src/ClearPluginAssemblies/bin/Release/net11.0/ClearPluginAssemblies.dll src/Build/
cp -f src/Build/src/ClearPluginAssemblies/bin/Release/net11.0/ClearPluginAssemblies.runtimeconfig.json src/Build/
```

MSB3073 / exit code 150 from plugin builds usually means a stale runtimeconfig still targeting the previous `netX.0`.
